Article 11 (Military Support Headquarters)
(1) The Military Support Headquarters shall have one director, who shall be a general officer. <Amended on September 5, 2017>
(2) The director shall be responsible for:
1. Determination of personnel and logistical resource requirements for operations and assessment of readiness;
2. Command and control systems, information and communications systems, military frequencies, interoperability of command communications, and information security;
3. Deleted <February 16, 2015>;
4. Operation of combat units dispatched overseas and their predeployment training;
5. Civil-military operations and martial law affairs. <Amended on February 16, 2015; December 30, 2022>
